            {
              "id": "679e06e4-f3af-35e9-a8a4-ed0e352cd95d",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis detected a possible undefined behavior risk due to overlapping memory regions between the source and destination in a memory copy operation. The code uses pointer arithmetic and type casting, making it difficult to guarantee that the source and destination do not overlap. Dataflow analysis suggests that the destination may be derived from the source, increasing the likelihood of overlap. Additionally, there are no explicit checks or guards in the code to prevent this condition. The source pointer could also be null, which further increases the risk of undefined behavior. These factors indicate a real risk of memory corruption or unpredictable program behavior if the overlap occurs.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo prevent undefined behavior when the source and destination memory regions may overlap, replace the memory copy operation with a function that safely handles overlapping regions, such as `memmove`. `memmove` is specifically designed to handle overlapping memory areas without causing corruption or undefined behavior. \n\n**Remediation Example:**\n\n```cpp\nstd::memmove((reinterpret_cast<address>(dst) + dstOffs), (reinterpret_cast<const_address>(hostPtr) + srcOffs), size[0] * elementSize_);\n```\n\nThis change ensures that even if the source and destination regions overlap, the data will be copied correctly and safely.\n\n## References\n- [OWASP: Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
